cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this work, please cite it as below.
title: "Chest X-Ray Domain-Shift & Shortcut-Learning Audit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pareddy"
    given-names: "Charith Reddy"
date-released: "2026-08-27"
url: "https://github.com/Charith-Reddy-Pareddy/medical-image-classification-for-disease-detection"
abstract: >
  An honors case study auditing pneumonia classifiers (a from-scratch CNN,
  ResNet-50, and DenseNet-121) trained on a single pediatric institution
  and evaluated without retraining on two independent adult-population
  chest X-ray datasets. Quantifies domain-shift degradation with
  bootstrapped confidence intervals and McNemar's test, and measures
  shortcut-feature reliance via a Grad-CAM-vs-lung-segmentation overlap
  metric with a border-masking ablation and causal analysis of what
  predicts it.
keywords:
  - medical imaging
  - domain shift
  - shortcut learning
  - chest x-ray
  - pneumonia detection
  - grad-cam
  - pytorch
license: MIT
